@startuml 07-implantacao-docker
title Diagrama de Implantação (Docker)

node "Servidor de Produção" {
  node "Container: ufsj_web" as Web {
    component "Next.js App\n(porta 3000)" as WebApp
  }

  node "Container: ufsj_postgres" as Postgres {
    database "PostgreSQL 16" as PG
  }

  node "Container: ufsj_redis" as Redis {
    queue "Redis 7" as RedisQ
  }

  node "Worker Python\n(fora do docker-compose atual)" as WorkerNode #LightYellow {
    component "worker-ia" as WorkerApp
  }
}

cloud "Google Drive API" as Drive
cloud "Gemini API" as Gemini

WebApp --> PG : DATABASE_URL
WebApp --> RedisQ : REDIS_URL (enfileira jobs)
WorkerApp --> RedisQ : consome jobs
WorkerApp --> PG : atualiza certificados\n(conexão direta)
WorkerApp --> Drive : download de arquivos
WorkerApp --> Gemini : análise de certificados
WebApp --> Drive : upload de arquivos

note bottom of WorkerNode
  Observação: o docker-compose.yml atual
  só define web, postgres e redis.
  O worker-ia ainda roda fora do compose
  (gap de infraestrutura a ser resolvido).
end note

@enduml
